WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.930
Nestvane runs Android

00:00:01.742 --> 00:00:03.439
17 inside an

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.583
ordinary iPhone app

00:00:05.118 --> 00:00:06.698
The open-source Nestvane

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.419
rebuilds Android 17

00:00:08.231 --> 00:00:09.351
from AOSP

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.684
translates it ahead

00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:11.521
of time and

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:12.393
ships it signed

00:00:12.205 --> 00:00:13.549
inside an iOS

00:00:13.361 --> 00:00:13.891
app.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:15.825
Because iOS apps

00:00:15.637 --> 00:00:17.287
cannot create executable

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:17.712
memory

00:00:17.806 --> 00:00:19.304
JIT and hypervisors

00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:20.011
are ruled out

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:22.004
Nestvane instead translates

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:22.853
Android ahead of

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:23.254
time

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:23.997
and adds a

00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:25.046
Linux kernel layer

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.530
written for the

00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:25.860
app.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.309
You can install

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:27.923
APKs

00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:28.807
use them with

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:29.786
touch and keep

00:00:29.598 --> 00:00:30.576
their data between

00:00:30.388 --> 00:00:31.071
launches

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.262
with widgets and

00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:33.665
720p video at

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:35.033
30 fps

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.564
Full story on

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:37.271
the dashboard
